From e03a48967d7f06cb0a99be4c5fdc613b7f6dec4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:24:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Map external touchscreens to the external monitor

Mutter maps a touchscreen to the monitor whose EDID vendor appears in the
device name or whose physical size matches the device; with neither, the
touchscreen goes to the built-in panel. The touch layer of a USB-C
portable monitor usually matches neither, so its touches land on the
tablet's own panel. Android maps external touchscreens to the external
display (TouchInputMapper, associatedDisplayIsExternal).

While exactly one monitor other than the built-in panel is connected,
give every USB or Bluetooth touchscreen that monitor as its configured
output, and reset the setting otherwise. This replaces an extension
that the user's extension settings could turn off; it runs in every
session mode, including the login and lock screens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
